    "JurisdictionSpecifics":  "Wisconsin. Self-defense is an affirmative defense under Wis. Stat. � 939.48. The defendant must produce evidence of self-defense; once raised, the State must disprove self-defense beyond a reasonable doubt. First-degree reckless homicide under Wis. Stat. � 940.02(1) requires proof that the defendant recklessly caused the death of another under circumstances showing utter disregard for human life.",
