    "Instructions":  {
                         "Text":  "Ladies and gentlemen of the jury, you are instructed as follows:\n\nThe defendant, Nicolae Miu, is charged with one count of First-Degree Reckless Homicide under Wisconsin Statute � 940.02(1), and four counts of First-Degree Recklessly Endangering Safety under Wisconsin Statute � 941.30(1).\n\nFirst-Degree Reckless Homicide requires the State to prove beyond a reasonable doubt: (1) the defendant caused the death of Isaac Schuman; (2) the defendant acted with criminally reckless conduct; and (3) the circumstances of the defendant�s conduct showed utter disregard for human life.\n\nFirst-Degree Recklessly Endangering Safety requires the State to prove beyond a reasonable doubt: (1) the defendant endangered the safety of another human being; (2) the defendant acted with criminally reckless conduct; and (3) the circumstances showed utter disregard for human life.\n\nThe defendant has raised the affirmative defense of self-defense. Under Wisconsin law, a person is privileged to threaten or intentionally use force against another if the person reasonably believes that such force is necessary to prevent imminent death or great bodily harm to himself. The defendant may not use force that is intended or likely to cause death or great bodily harm unless the person reasonably believes that such force is necessary to prevent imminent death or great bodily harm to himself.\n\nOnce the issue of self-defense is raised, the State must prove beyond a reasonable doubt that the defendant did NOT act in self-defense. You must find the defendant not guilty if you are not satisfied beyond a reasonable doubt that the defendant did not act in self-defense.\n\nYou are the sole judges of the credibility of witnesses and the weight to be given to the evidence. You must deliberate together and reach a unanimous verdict on each count. Your verdict must be based solely on the evidence presented and these instructions of law.",
                         "Standard":  "BeyondReasonableDoubt"
                     },
