                     {
                         "FileName":  "Cell Phone Video - Confrontation.mp4",
                         "FilePath":  "",
                         "Summary":  "A 3-minute cell phone video recorded by a tuber showing the confrontation on the Apple River. The video shows Miu approaching a group of tubers, a verbal exchange escalating, individuals shoving Miu, Miu being pushed underwater, and then Miu emerging with a knife and stabbing multiple people in quick succession. The video captures chaotic shouting and screaming. Key disputed moments: whether Miu was the initial aggressor, whether he had space to retreat, and whether the level of force was proportionate to the threat.",
                         "AdmittedAt":  "2024-04-08T09:00:00",
                         "ExhibitNumber":  1,
                         "EvidenceStrength":  0.48,
                         "IsDiscoveryComplete":  true,
                         "ClerkNotes":  "Central exhibit. Video clearly shows Miu being shoved and punched by multiple individuals before the knife appears. While interpretations differ, the visual evidence of Miu being physically attacked first is compelling for the defense.",
                         "MediaType":  "Document",
                         "OfferingAttorney":  "District Attorney Karl Anderson",
                         "IsOfferedByPlaintiffSide":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "FileName":  "Autopsy Report - Isaac Schuman.pdf",
                         "FilePath":  "",
                         "Summary":  "Medical examiner\u0027s report confirming that Isaac Schuman, 17, died from a single stab wound to the chest penetrating the heart. The wound was 3.5 inches deep. Toxicology showed Schuman\u0027s blood alcohol content was 0.23%, nearly three times the legal limit for driving. Defense emphasizes that someone this intoxicated could be an unpredictable and dangerous physical threat. No other drugs detected.",
                         "AdmittedAt":  "2024-04-08T10:30:00",
                         "ExhibitNumber":  2,
                         "EvidenceStrength":  0.52,
                         "EstimatedDamages":  0.0,
                         "IsDiscoveryComplete":  true,
                         "ClerkNotes":  "Undisputed cause of death. High BAC level (0.23%) strengthens defense argument that the victims were dangerously intoxicated and aggressive. A reasonable person could fear serious harm from someone this impaired.",
                         "MediaType":  "Document",
                         "OfferingAttorney":  "District Attorney Karl Anderson",
                         "IsOfferedByPlaintiffSide":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "FileName":  "Miu Police Interview Transcript.pdf",
                         "FilePath":  "",
                         "Summary":  "Transcript of Nicolae Miu\u0027s voluntary interview with police on the day of the incident. Miu consistently states he was tubing with his wife, lost his phone, and approached a group to ask if they had seen it. He describes being surrounded by 8-10 hostile, intoxicated individuals, being shoved underwater, and genuinely fearing for his life. He admits pulling out his pocket knife and swinging to create space. His account has remained consistent from the first police interview through trial. His emotional distress appears genuine throughout the recording.",
                         "AdmittedAt":  "2024-04-09T09:00:00",
                         "ExhibitNumber":  3,
                         "EvidenceStrength":  0.49,
                         "IsDiscoveryComplete":  true,
                         "ClerkNotes":  "Consistent account from day one. Voluntary interview. Miu\u0027s description of being surrounded and fearing for his life has remained unchanged.",
                         "MediaType":  "Document",
                         "OfferingAttorney":  "District Attorney Karl Anderson",
                         "IsOfferedByPlaintiffSide":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "FileName":  "Medical Records - Surviving Victims.pdf",
                         "FilePath":  "",
                         "Summary":  "Medical records for the four surviving stabbing victims: Dante Carlson (stab wound to abdomen, surgery), Tony Carlson (stab wound to chest wall, punctured lung), Alex Martin (stab wound to arm, nerve damage), and Rhyley Mattison (superficial stab wound to back). Crucially, all four had elevated blood alcohol levels (0.15% to 0.28%). Defense argues that facing a group of highly intoxicated, aggressive young men justifies Miu\u0027s fear of serious bodily harm. The pattern of wounds — quick, panicked strikes rather than targeted attacks — supports Miu\u0027s account of swinging wildly to escape.",
                         "AdmittedAt":  "2024-04-09T11:00:00",
                         "ExhibitNumber":  4,
                         "EvidenceStrength":  0.51,
                         "IsDiscoveryComplete":  true,
                         "ClerkNotes":  "BAC levels across all victims strongly support defense narrative of an intoxicated, hostile mob. Injury pattern is consistent with panicked self-defense rather than targeted violence.",
                         "MediaType":  "Document",
                         "OfferingAttorney":  "District Attorney Karl Anderson",
                         "IsOfferedByPlaintiffSide":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "FileName":  "Defense Expert - Use of Force Analysis.pdf",
                         "FilePath":  "",
                         "Summary":  "Defense-retained use-of-force expert (former law enforcement, 25 years) analyzed the video and concluded: (1) Miu was surrounded by 6-8 individuals; (2) Miu was physically assaulted — punched, shoved, pushed underwater — before any knife was visible; (3) A 52-year-old man facing multiple younger, intoxicated men reasonably feared imminent death or great bodily harm; (4) The disparity of force (one vs. many) and age differential (52 vs. early 20s) supports a reasonable belief in the need for deadly force; (5) The entire incident lasted approximately 40 seconds, leaving no time for calculated decisions. Cross-examination focused on payment, but credentials and analysis were not effectively impeached.",
                         "AdmittedAt":  "2024-04-10T09:00:00",
                         "ExhibitNumber":  5,
                         "EvidenceStrength":  0.52,
                         "IsDiscoveryComplete":  true,
